Release	Format GitHub release notes	2026-11-25T13:39:29.9806378Z {"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/universal-translator/releases/458166658","assets_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/universal-translator/releases/458166658/assets","upload_url":"https://uploads.github.com/repos/link-foundation/universal-translator/releases/458166658/assets{?name,label}","html_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/universal-translator/releases/tag/v0.14.0","id":458166658,"author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"node_id":"RE_kwDOVJ4SV84bTxGC","tag_name":"v0.14.0","target_commitish":"main","name":"@link-foundation/universal-translator 0.14.0","draft":false,"immutable":false,"prerelease":false,"created_at":"2026-11-25T13:37:11Z","updated_at":"2026-11-25T13:39:29Z","published_at":"2026-11-25T13:39:27Z","assets":[],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/universal-translator/tarball/v0.14.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/universal-translator/zipball/v0.14.0","body":"Language versions, standards of one's own, a comment language and concrete syntax trees by default.\n- `formatMeta` shows the meta program as Links Notation, so the meta language of any text can be seen.\n- Every language has a single entry with versions:\n- programming languages have major versions (`python@2`);\n- natural languages have regional spellings (British English, chosen from the browser languages), smaller vocabularies down to the semantic primes, and controlled standards.\n- The 65 semantic primes are given for every supported natural language, as a `minimal-<language>` version of each.\n- Every word of a language's vocabulary can be changed and saved as a version of one's own (`languageVocabulary`, `vocabularyChanges`, `writeLanguageVersion`, `loadLanguageVersion`). Every changed word takes effect.\n- Word standards hold up to 1024 words. New words are defined through the words a standard already has, recursively, with Wikidata lookups through a cache and an offline pre-cache (`createStandard`, `defineWord`, `wikidataLookup`).\n- Comments can be translated into another natural language apart from the code (`commentLanguage`).\n- Whitespace and comments are kept as written:\n- the spaces inside comments;\n- empty lines between statements and between functions, or the lack of them;\n- trailing comments;\n- comments that close an indented block.\n- The web demo:\n- shows the meta language of both texts;\n- translates the right text into a newly chosen left language instead of failing;\n- generates random Program, Function and Statement examples;\n- has a Standards tab and a settings panel built on link-foundation/ui with themes, skins and seven interface languages.\n- Comment languages and language versions work with partial translation, the source language `auto`, `--all-or-nothing` and rules as data. A comment language that does not exist is refused before reading, and reading a version such as `python@2` uses the rules of its language.\n- The Rust crate has the same language versions, natural language versions, comment languages and `--comment-language`/`--comment-from` flags.\n\n**Related Pull Request:** #7\n\n---\n\n[![npm version](https://img.shields.io/badge/npm-0.14.0-blue.svg)](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@link-foundation/universal-translator/v/0.14.0)"}✅ Formatted release notes for v0.14.0
